  << /ActualText (Technique Highlight 1\072 \nEnvironmental Guidance Through Light\050\050My Method\072 I used red emergency lighting as the primary navigation system throughout the level\056 Rather than waypoints or minimaps\054 the red light acts as a silent guide \024 players follow it instinctively without being told to\056\050\050How I Executed It\072 Red light is present at every key decision point and transition\056 In Beat 3 I deliberately removed the red light cue temporarily to create disorientation and tension\056 When it reappears\054 the relief the player feels reinforces how much they had come to rely on it\056\050\050Level Example\072 The notice board in Beat 1 explicitly states \042Follow Red Light For Emergency Exit\042 \024 establishing the rule early so the rest of the level can use it without explanation\056\050)
     /K [ 39 ]
     /P 3617 0 R
