3624 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Beat 1 \024 Orientation\050Tower 2 Interior \174 No Combat \174 Low Intensity\050\050The level opens in a flickering red emergency light\056 The player is immediately blocked from going back \024 the entrance is collapsed behind them\056 A notice board ahead delivers the only explicit instruction of the entire level\072 follow the red light for emergency exit\056 From this point forward the red light becomes the player\047s silent guide\056\050\050The first section is entirely movement focused\056 Walk\054 run\054 jump\054 ledge grab\054 torch\054 crouch\054 crawl \024 each mechanic is introduced in sequence through the environment\054 each one required to progress\056 Two paths appear offering different movement approaches but leading to the same destination\056 A road block ends the beat\054 forcing the player to find an alternate route upward\056\n\n\n\050\050\050\050Beat 2 \024 First Contact\050Tower 2 Upper Floors \174 Stealth \053 Combat Introduction \174 Low \222 Medium Intensity\050\050The player opens a door into a storage area and is forced to pick up a note\056 The message is urgent \024 the prison has been taken over\054 mafia gunmen are sweeping every block\054 stay alert and move quiet\056 This is the first narrative beat and the first time the player understands the full danger of their situation\056\050\050Exiting storage the player encounters the first enemy \024 harmless until approached\054 with a monologue prompt and a clear instruction to eliminate\056 After the takedown\054 a weapon storage room rewards the player with ammo\054 firearms\054 and practice dummies\056 Two path options appear before the first real combat \024 a pair of armed enemies guarding the upper floor\056 After clearing them the player discovers a blocked route\054 finds a way upward through ledge climbing\054 and the beat ends\056\050\050\050\050\n\nBeat 3 \024 Into the Dark\050Tower 2 Cell Block \174 Exploration \053 Traversal \174 Medium Intensity\050\050Two landing choices greet the player \024 one path rewards with a silenced weapon\054 the other gives progression only\056 This is the first pure risk versus reward decision\056 Neither path is signposted \024 the player must explore to discover what each offers\056\050\050Tight spaces create genuine stress\056 A relief moment opens into a larger area with a visible exit nearby\056 Ladder climbing is introduced\056 The red light disappears \024 the player feels lost and uncertain\056 New pathways through the cell block eventually reveal red light traces again\056 The beat ends with the player back on track but having experienced real disorientation for the first time\056\050\050\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\050\050Beat 4 \024 The World Opens\050Tower 3 Office Floors \174 Escalating Combat \053 Discovery \174 Medium \222 High Intensity\050\050A risky slide down a slanted platform opens Beat 4 with immediate physical stakes\056 Three path choices appear \024 one familiar blocked route from Beat 3\054 one reward only path with an AK\05547\054 and one progression path\056 The environment shifts from prison cells to office space \024 the world of the prison is expanding\056\050\050A bridge connecting towers triggers a monologue and delivers the level\047s first full exterior view\056 Tower 1 and Tower 4 are visible and labelled \024 the player understands the full scale of the environment for the first time\056 Back inside the office\054 a dark room forces torch use and rewards with a sniper rifle\056 High tension followed by high reward \024 the beat ends with the player well\055armed and moving forward\056\050\050\n\n\n\050\050Beat 5 \024 Point of No Return\050Tower 3 Control Room \053 Ground Floor \174 Puzzle \053 Narrative Climax \174 High Intensity\050\050Red light returns\054 restoring player confidence\056 A large slant drops the player to ground level \024 the first time they have been at street level\056 A monologue confirms there is no direct way out\056 Exploration reveals a ledge climbing route with a new variation keeping traversal fresh\056\050\050The control room is the narrative heart of the level\056 A button opens a door remotely\056 Security monitors show escape platforms ahead \024 a visual reward for curious players who look closely\056 A fax document on the desk delivers the clearest objective of the entire level\072 Tower 1 Helipad\054 last scheduled extraction\054 proceed without delay\056 A monologue confirms there is no going back\056 An interactable object reveals a vent escape route\056 The player lands at ground level with the door open and enemies ahead\056 The final push begins\056\050\050\n\n\nBeat 6 \024 Extraction\050Ground Level \053 Tower 4 \053 Tower 1 \174 Final Combat \053 Dual Path Climax \174 High \222 Climax\050\050A patrolling armed enemy greets the player at the exit \024 the most dangerous surprise encounter of the level\056 Stealth or combat\054 the choice is immediate and consequential\056\050\050Two routes to extraction exist from this point\056 The stealth path uses cover objects on a bridge\054 requires full crouch navigation\054 and demands one final elimination before reaching a zipline connecting Tower 4 to Tower 1\056 The combat path clears ground level aggressively\054 climbs toward the opposite bridge\054 eliminates one more enemy\054 and reaches the same final ladder\056 Both paths converge at the Tower 4 exterior climbing trail\054 leading to the rooftop\056 From there Tower 1 is visible\056 A final climb delivers the player to the helipad\056 Extraction complete\056\050\050)
     /K [ 43 ]
     /P 3625 0 R
     /Pg 3538 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

