3732 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Technical Challenges\050\050Two significant technical problems were encountered during development\056\050\050The first was lighting management across indoor and outdoor spaces\056 Balancing the atmospheric red emergency lighting indoors against the natural daylight of the exterior environment required continuous iteration to maintain visual consistency and player readability across both contexts\056\050\050The second was working with AGLS \024 the Advanced Game Locomotion System\056 Documentation was limited and the system was complex\056 Key features required significant time to understand and implement correctly\056 One major gap was the absence of a health pickup system within AGLS \024 the system architecture made adding one prohibitively time\055consuming\056\050\050Rather than spending development time solving a complex technical problem\054 I made a design decision\072 I restructured the level progression so that even a player with low combat skill would not lose health frequently\056 Enemy encounters were reduced in number\054 combat sequences were simplified\054 and the focus was placed firmly on level design\054 traversal\054 and pacing\056 This constraint ultimately strengthened the design \024 forcing clarity and intention in every encounter rather than relying on combat volume\056)
     /K [ 97 ]
     /P 3733 0 R
     /Pg 3538 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

3733 0 obj
  << /K [ 3732 0 R ]
     /P 3738 0 R
     /S /P
     /Pg 3538 0 R
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

3734 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Reflection\nAcross playtesting\054 the level kept proving itself in small moments\056\nIn Beat 1\054 players found the hidden passage on their own \024 the closed stairs and the flashlight nearby were enough to guide them without a single prompt\056 After Beat 1\054 players naturally looked for an alternative route when the bridge was blocked\054 exactly as the design intended\056 By Beat 5\054 most testers climbed through the ledge sequence without hesitation \024 a sequence I had deliberately made more complex than anything before it\054 requiring camera movement and grabbing simultaneously\056 They figured it out because the earlier beats had already built that instinct in them\056\nThat progression \024 players carrying skills forward without realising it \024 was the clearest sign the level was working as a whole\056)
     /K [ 98 ]
     /P 3735 0 R
     /Pg 3538 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

3735 0 obj
  << /K [ 3734 0 R ]
