3736 0 obj
  << /ActualText (What I Would Do Differently\nGiven more time\054 the first priority would be a proper health and inventory system\056 The absence of health pickups in AGLS forced a design workaround \024 structuring encounters so players rarely died rather than giving them tools to survive a harder fight\056 A full system would have opened the door to more competitive survival scenarios and richer resource management\056\nMore time would also mean larger spaces\056 With that constraint removed\054 exploration sections could expand significantly \024 giving the narrative more room and rewarding thorough players with richer environmental storytelling\056\nPrisonBreak\137LD is the foundation of something bigger\056 The core systems work\056 The next step is building on this prototype with the production features it needs to become a complete experience\056)
     /K [ 99 ]
     /P 3737 0 R
     /Pg 3538 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

